<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka tenders to sell July fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka tenders to sell July fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 18,000-20,000 tonnes of 180-cst fuel oil, a company source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender, which offers the 3.5-percent fuel oil for lifting July 22-23, will close on July 15 and bids will be valid for two days, the source said.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold the same amount of 177-cst, 3.5-percent fuel oil at a discount of $12.50 per tonne to Singapore spot quotes for late May lifting on a free-on-board Colombo basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
</text>
